# Parallel Feature Development

> When multiple agents work on separate feature branches simultaneously,
> coordination prevents integration pain. This rule is **mandatory** for
> every agent operating in a worktree.

## Worktree Inventory

`STATUS.md` is the single source of truth for active work. Every agent
**must** maintain the **Active Worktrees** table:

```markdown
## Active Worktrees

| Branch | Worktree Dir | Ticket | Agent | Status | Files Touched |
|--------|-------------|--------|-------|--------|---------------|
| feat/{{TICKET_PREFIX}}-NNN-auth | {{PROJECT_NAME}}--{{TICKET_PREFIX}}-NNN | {{TICKET_PREFIX}}-NNN | Claude | in-progress | core/security.py, api/v1/auth.py |
| feat/{{TICKET_PREFIX}}-NNN-rate-limit | {{PROJECT_NAME}}--{{TICKET_PREFIX}}-NNN | {{TICKET_PREFIX}}-NNN | Cursor | in-progress | core/middleware.py, main.py |
```

Rules:
- **Session start**: Read the table. Note which files other branches touch
- **Session end**: Update your row (status, files touched)
- **On merge**: Remove your row from the table

## Sync Protocol

### 1. Daily Rebase (Session Start)

Every session must begin with a sync against `master`:

```bash
git fetch origin
git rebase origin/master
```

- If rebase succeeds: continue working
- If rebase conflicts: resolve, run full test suite, then continue
- If conflicts are non-trivial (>3 files or touching unfamiliar code): **stop and ask the user**

### 2. Pre-Merge Sync (Before PR)

Before opening or merging a PR, perform the **full sync ritual**:

```bash
# 1. Fetch latest master
git fetch origin

# 2. Rebase on master (no merge commits in feature branches)
git rebase origin/master

# 3. Run the full test suite
PYTHONPATH=. .venv/bin/pytest

# 4. Run pre-commit on all files (not just staged)
pre-commit run --all-files

# 5. Force-push the rebased branch
git push --force-with-lease origin HEAD
```

All five steps must pass. If any step fails, fix before proceeding.

### 3. Post-Merge Cascade

When **any** feature branch merges into `master`:

1. The merging agent removes its row from the Active Worktrees table
2. All other active worktrees must rebase on the new `master` at their
   next session start (enforced by rule 1 above)
3. If your branch touches files that the merged branch also touched
   (check the "Files Touched" column), rebase **immediately** — do not
   continue working on a stale base

## Merge Ordering

When multiple branches are ready to merge simultaneously:

| Scenario | Order |
|----------|-------|
| Independent features (no shared files) | First-ready merges first |
| Shared file overlap | Smaller/simpler change merges first |
| Explicit dependency (branch B needs branch A) | Dependency merges first |
| Both touch shared infra (config, deps, middleware) | **Ask user** for merge order |

After each merge, wait for CI to pass on `master` before merging the next branch.
Never merge two branches into `master` back-to-back without CI confirmation.

## Conflict Prevention

- **Keep features small**: One ticket = one concern. Avoid mega-branches
- **Isolate shared changes**: If your feature requires changes to shared
  infrastructure (config, deps, base classes, middleware), extract those
  into a dedicated branch, merge it first, then rebase your feature on top
- **Communicate via the table**: Update "Files Touched" whenever you
  modify a new file. This is the early-warning system for other agents
- **Lock files**: If two branches must modify the same file extensively,
  one branch should wait for the other to merge first. Note this in the
  "Status" column as `waiting-on-{{TICKET_PREFIX}}-NNN`

## Migration Conflicts

Alembic migrations are a special case — two branches cannot both add
migrations without conflicts:

- Only **one** branch at a time should contain an Alembic migration
- If your feature needs a migration and another active branch already
  has one, add yours **after** that branch merges
- If both need migrations urgently: ask the user to coordinate the
  merge order, then regenerate the later migration after rebase

## Worktree Lifecycle

```
1. CREATE  → git worktree add ../{{PROJECT_NAME}}--{{TICKET_PREFIX}}-NNN master
                              → ln -s "$(pwd)/.venv" ../{{PROJECT_NAME}}--{{TICKET_PREFIX}}-NNN/.venv
                              → Add row to Active Worktrees table
2. WORK    → Normal development with daily rebase
3. PRE-PR  → Full sync ritual (section 2 above)
4. MERGE   → Auto-merge workflow (from git.md)
                              → Remove row from Active Worktrees table
5. CLEANUP → git worktree remove ../{{PROJECT_NAME}}--{{TICKET_PREFIX}}-NNN
```
